		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3586&amp;p=28084#p28084"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Announcements • Forum registration is now only if you have a callsign]]></title>

					<category term="Announcements" scheme="http://localhost/opengd77/viewforum.php?f=3" label="Announcements"/>
		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3586&amp;p=28084#p28084"><![CDATA[
Because of the massive problem we had with thousands of bots registering on the site, we had to manually cull about 2000 bot accounts in September &amp;October 2023.<br><br>Following these deletions, all new account names must be people's registered callsign, which are verified against QRZ.com other reputable sources<br><br>Any registration which does not pass this test will be automatically deleted.<br><br>OpenGD77 is not the only forum which has needed to enforce registration rules,  PiStar forum also seems to require callsigns.<br><br>I know this prevents non-Hams from registering on the site, but the site is fully accessible to everyone, unlike many social media groups which are private.<br><br>And despite it being clearly stated in the registration page, that you must enter a valid callsign, we continue to average 5 invalid callsign registration attempts per day<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Dec 14, 2023 10:13 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
