		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Announcements • Baofeng DM-1701, DM-1802, RT-84 and TYT MD-2017 / RT-92]]></title>

					<category term="Announcements" scheme="http://localhost/opengd77/viewforum.php?f=3" label="Announcements"/>
		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2712&amp;p=22316#p22316"><![CDATA[
Thanks to the work of BD4VOW we are now developing a version of the firmware for the Baofeng DM-1701<br><br>It also looks likely that we will be able to develop a version which works on the TYT MD-2017 / Retevis RT-91<br><br>Currently the DM-1701 version still has some problems with the user interface keypad mapping, but we hope to improve this as soon as the DM-1701 which I ordered on 4th March arrives.<br><br>The latest firmware for the DM-1701 can be downloaded from here<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/DM1701/Firmware/Latest/" class="postlink">downloads/DM1701/Firmware/Latest/</a><br><br><br>The CPS is already being modified to support loading firmware onto these radios.<br><br>See the version of the CPS with the newest date in <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/CPS/Latest/" class="postlink">downloads/CPS/Latest/</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Mar 04, 2023 9:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
